  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 6,
    "summary": "Job bemoans his grief—He prays that God will grant his petitions—Those who are afflicted should be pitied—How forcible are right words!",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "But Job answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Oh that my grief were throughly weighed, and my calamity laid in the balances together!",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Despair."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Despair.",
            "prettyString": "TG Despair",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Despair",
                "entryId": "tg-despair",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For now it would be heavier than the sand of the sea: therefore my words are swallowed up.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "For the arrows of the Almighty are within me, the poison whereof drinketh up my spirit: the terrors of God do set themselves in array against me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Doth the wild ass bray when he hath grass? or loweth the ox over his fodder?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Can that which is unsavoury be eaten without salt? or is there any taste in the white of an egg?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "The things that my soul refused to touch are as my sorrowful meat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Oh that I might have my request; and that God would grant me the thing that I long for!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Even that it would please God to destroy me; that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Then should I yet have comfort; yea, I would harden myself in sorrow: let him not spare; for I have not concealed the words of the Holy One.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "What is my strength, that I should hope? and what is mine end, that I should prolong my life?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Is my strength the strength of stones? or is my flesh of brass?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Is not my help in me? and is wisdom driven quite from me?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "To him that is afflicted pity should be shewed from his friend; but he forsaketh the fear of the Almighty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Compassion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 46
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Compassion.",
            "prettyString": "TG Compassion",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Compassion",
                "entryId": "tg-compassion",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "My brethren have dealt deceitfully as a brook, and as the stream of brooks they pass away;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Which are blackish by reason of the ice, and wherein the snow is hid:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "What time they wax warm, they vanish: when it is hot, they are consumed out of their place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "The paths of their way are turned aside; they go to nothing, and perish.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The troops of Tema looked, the companies of Sheba waited for them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "HEB caravans."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "They were confounded because they had hoped; they came thither, and were ashamed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "For now ye are nothing; ye see my casting down, and are afraid.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Did I say, Bring unto me? or, Give a reward for me of your substance?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "IE Bring gifts."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Or, Deliver me from the enemy’s hand? or, Redeem me from the hand of the mighty?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Teach me, and I will hold my tongue: and cause me to understand wherein I have erred.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "How forcible are right words! but what doth your arguing reprove?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Do ye imagine to reprove words, and the speeches of one that is desperate, which are as wind?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, ye overwhelm the fatherless, and ye dig a pit for your friend.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "2 Ne. 28:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 47
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Ne. 28:8.",
            "prettyString": "2 Nephi 28:8",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 28,
                    "end": 28,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Now therefore be content, look upon me; for it is evident unto you if I lie.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Return, I pray you, let it not be iniquity; yea, return again, my righteousness is in it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Is there iniquity in my tongue? cannot my taste discern perverse things?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 6:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 6,
        "verse": 30
      }
    ]
